WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.870
- [Kelly] I wanna ask, you know, because

00:00:01.870 --> 00:00:03.850
we're now finally having
a real conversation

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:04.823
about white privilege.

00:00:04.823 --> 00:00:07.030
I actually watched a lot of things you do,

00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:09.770
and 'cause I'm a fan
of yours, but last year

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:11.157
you did a documentary called

00:00:11.157 --> 00:00:12.588
"Hello Privilege, It's Me, Chelsea"

00:00:12.588 --> 00:00:15.458
and you were way ahead
of the curve on that one.

00:00:15.458 --> 00:00:18.049
But what inspired you to do that,

00:00:18.049 --> 00:00:20.150
and what did you learn from it?

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:21.420
- [Chelsea] Well, I wrote, well,

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:25.330
I wrote my last book "Life
Will Be The Death Of Me"

00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:27.480
which was about going to therapy

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:28.670
for the first time in my life.

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:29.870
And when I did go to therapy

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:31.030
for the first time in my life,

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:32.940
after Trump was elected in 2016,

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:34.790
I had a lot of anger,

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:36.970
and I had a lot of rage
about him being elected,

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.420
and I didn't understand.

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:40.610
And so I had to do some
really deep digging

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:43.580
to A: what was going on with me

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:44.880
and my reaction to that,

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:47.490
and why I couldn't calmly discuss it,

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:49.070
you know, instead of like with my veins

00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:50.150
popping out of my neck,

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:52.129
and tweeting while I'm sleeping,

00:00:52.129 --> 00:00:54.796
trying to actually get
ahold of my emotions

00:00:54.796 --> 00:00:56.480
and be in a place where I'm

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:58.210
responding not reacting,

00:00:58.210 --> 00:00:59.713
you know, and through that work

00:00:59.713 --> 00:01:02.679
and like going to therapy
seriously for a while,

00:01:02.679 --> 00:01:05.920
I just, it was just, obvious to me

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:07.553
how I had failed to look around

00:01:07.553 --> 00:01:10.100
and see how the color of my skin

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:12.012
has been such a benefit to my own success.

00:01:12.012 --> 00:01:14.380
So I was very interested
in doing a documentary

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:17.830
about finding out what
does white privilege mean?

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:18.732
Because to me it just meant

00:01:18.732 --> 00:01:19.927
people who go to Harvard

00:01:19.927 --> 00:01:22.391
or go to those, you
know, Ivy League schools

00:01:22.391 --> 00:01:24.033
or the Rockefellers.

00:01:24.033 --> 00:01:25.825
I thought that was white privilege

00:01:25.825 --> 00:01:28.390
when I started that documentary.

00:01:28.390 --> 00:01:31.415
And then you learn that,
no, you don't have to

00:01:31.415 --> 00:01:33.390
go to an Ivy League school,

00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:34.252
your family doesn't have to be wealthy,

00:01:34.252 --> 00:01:37.010
for it to be a privilege
to have white skin.

00:01:37.010 --> 00:01:38.465
You are benefiting from a system

00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:40.810
that other people - that is hurting

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:41.643
other people.

00:01:41.643 --> 00:01:42.755
As long as people are hurting,

00:01:42.755 --> 00:01:45.230
then there is a group of people that are

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:46.230
benefiting from that.

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:47.297
That's just the way it works.

00:01:47.297 --> 00:01:49.540
And so it opened my eyes so much,

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:51.020
and I just loved that film,

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:52.055
and I had to say...

00:01:52.055 --> 00:01:53.970
It was a film to white people,

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:55.780
to say "Listen, I know these conversations

00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:58.180
are uncomfortable, but
we should be having them

00:01:58.180 --> 00:01:59.130
because we have a problem

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:00.390
in this country."

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:02.370
- [Kelly] And without
you being uncomfortable

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:04.220
I don't think change will even occur.

